# etc
#
# `_*` was unscoped and matched at EVERY depth, so it silently excluded all 11
# `spoof_superb/**/__init__.py`, `verification/__main__.py`, and
# `bin/_common.sh` -- i.e. the package did not import at all from a fresh clone
# and no bin/ script could source its preamble. Scoped to the repo root, which
# is where the scratch directories it was written for live, plus explicit
# re-includes so a future broad rule cannot take the package out again.
/_*
!**/__init__.py
!**/__main__.py
!bin/_common.sh
/.codex
exp_result/
# Root-scoped: checkpoint directories live at the repo root. Unscoped, this also
# matched `spoof_superb/models/`, which is source -- its .py files survived only
# because they had been force-added before the rule landed, while
# `models/__init__.py` never was and so never shipped.
/models/
depreciated/
LA/
/home/suryasss/speaker-specific-ASD/__pycache__/*
saved_model/*

